    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint now accepts an optional `birthDate` and the owner responses (both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`) expose a derived `ageBand`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `birthDate` (optional ISO date) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are code-generated, so this produces `OwnerDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter, so the value survives the create\u2192fetch round-trip.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`AgeBand.java`** (new mapper helper) \u2014 Computes the band as full years from `birthDate` to `registrationDate` (`Period.between`): `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u226565 \u2192 SENIOR`; returns `null` when no birthDate was supplied. Kept standalone (like the existing `CheckDigit`/`CustomerCode` helpers) so MapStruct doesn't treat it as a mapping method.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired `ageBand` via an expression calling `AgeBand.of(owner)`, matching how `locality`, `contactPreference`, `checkDigit`, etc. are derived. `birthDate` maps automatically by name from `OwnerFieldsDto` \u2192 `Owner`.\n\nComputing `ageBand` in the mapper means it's derived consistently on every response (create and GET) from the persisted `birthDate` and `registrationDate`, rather than being stored redundantly. The band is deliberately computed against `registrationDate` (which is resolved/defaulted earlier in the pipeline), per the spec.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01`, registrationDate defaulting to today \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
